(TIM-56 - `Start` applied to something that is not a timer is a compile
 error, so a generated program cannot start a number by accident.
 Note where the diagnostic points: at the DECLARATION of `counter` on line
 1, not at the offending `Start` on line 2. Recorded because it will
 mislead anyone triaging a generated program that fails to compile.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-56.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Start requires a timer: counter
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a number called counter is 3.
Start the counter.
print counter.
